{
  "$comment": "One entry per menu item and app command (plan §4.4). `frontend` entries are app commands: the TS registry (src/commands/registry.ts) attaches enabled/run, the native menu (src-tauri/src/menu) lists them. `predefined` entries are the OS's own items (copy, quit...) on the `platforms` listed; `shortcut` records the accelerator the OS gives them so the duplicate-shortcut checks see it. Entry order is menu order. `menu: app` is the macOS application menu; `menuElsewhere` places an app entry on Windows/Linux. `menuAccelerators`: where the native menu items carry the app commands' accelerators (shown, and run only if a key reaches the menu - the page claims every app key first, src/commands/shortcuts.ts); off where the menu could see a key before the page or until the platform's smoke checklist passes. `shortcutAlias`: a second key only the page binds (the menu cannot match it), e.g. ⌘+ beside Zoom In's ⌘=. Zoom input has one owner per platform: the view.zoom* commands on macOS/Linux (`zoomHotkeysEnabled` off in tauri.conf.json), WebView2 on Windows (on in tauri.windows.conf.json; the page binds no zoom key there). Shortcut grammar: src/commands/keys.ts.",
